MoBetta: x87sidecar: Bridge x87 runs across flag-dead shifts by an immediate.

Run bridging v2 carries one IR run across add/sub/and/or/xor/inc/dec whose
written flags Rosetta's liveness proves dead, but not across shifts. WoW
3.3.5a's box-vs-frustum test (0x9839e0) picks each box corner with
`mov eax,[plane]; shr eax,31; mov eax,[ebp+eax*4-8]` between its x87 ops,
so its first four x87 ops went one per reply through the single-op path,
each converting its 80-bit slot in and out. In the Shadowglen inn at ultra
that block was 17.9% of the game's exec-weighted x87 ARM output.

shl/shr/sar r32/r64, imm now bridge under the same flag-dead proof, as
three more BridgeAluRI kinds lowered to UBFM/SBFM (LSL/LSR/ASR), which
never write NZCV. A count that masks to 0 stays with stock (x86 leaves the
register and flags alone there). CL counts and memory forms do not bridge.

That block: 586 -> 124 ARM per pass; whole inn capture 836G -> 709G
exec-weighted ARM (-15%). MoBetta tests/x87_bridge_shift.c: bit-identical
to stock Rosetta, the loop 993 -> 204 ms. In game: inn 90-100 -> 115-130 FPS.

